Thanks, durka! I'm willing to proceed in whichever direction BPFK 
indicates, i.e. marking the non-conforming words as obsolete, or applying 
changes to the words so that they conform. re: gleki's suggestion, once the 
changes have been applied for v135 (or v112951 per LMW), I'd be glad to 
consider a similar revision to the list of words marked obsolete by 
previous changes to the morphological rules. 

On Sunday, April 19, 2015 at 9:18:17 AM UTC-8, la durka wrote:
>
> This spreadsheet 
> <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1--fTZFzzlRo5WNPunLCz9VLrYdAOLAI33c3GIAkHoy8/edit?usp=sharing> shows 
> the words invalidated by the CGV rule and two possible ways to 
> automatically fix them: replacing {xua} with {xuua} (CVGV) or with {xu'a} 
> (CV'V), discounting words where that doesn't help (because the result is a 
> tosmabru or a lujvo, for example). I am not saying we should apply a 
> blanket fix without looking through the words, but it's useful to have this 
> list to look at.
>

